node_modules/
dist/
editor/dist/
.astro/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
# ...but NOT the committed placeholder. `.env.*` above swallows `.env.example`, and a
# swallowed placeholder never reaches a clone — "green from a clean clone" would then be
# false while looking true, which is the failure mode this tree refuses. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v .env.example`, which must exit 1.
!.env.example

# The content repository, when cloned inside this tree.
# The security argument for keeping code and content separate depends on editor-writable
# bytes never sitting beside build config; an accidental `git add` here would defeat it
# silently. The default
# location is a sibling directory (`../jamground-content`, JAMGROUND_CONTENT_DIR),
# but a clone placed here must not be committable back into the wrong repository.
/content
